00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:10.520
Asu, and A Class Visit

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:21.220
<i>This shirt is too childish.</i>

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:23.530
<i>This one and that one are, too.</i>

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:26.280
Parents’ day, huh?

00:04:33.950 --> 00:04:37.340
Ah, my mom’s here! Is yours here too, Kyou-chan?

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:40.370
My dad’s coming!

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:44.180
Rise.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:45.720
Bow.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:48.720
I guess dad’s still on his way.

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:52.140
All right! Who knows how to read this?

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:54.720
I do! I do! I do!

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.060
<i>He’s still not here…</i>

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:56.710
Let’s all read it together!

00:04:56.710 --> 00:05:00.900
In the end, Taro said,

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:03.670
<i>He’s just a little late. He’ll come for sure!</i>

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:05.850
“We can all definitely look forward to both the happy times and the sad times,

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:10.950
as they are feelings that come from the very bottom of your heart…”

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:09.520
<i>Dad, why didn’t you come?</i>

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:12.150
<i>You promised me!</i>

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:20.340
<i>Back then, I was jealous of everyone who just took it for granted that their parents would show up.</i>

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:27.310
<i>I missed Mom, who had gone to heaven, so much that I cried all night.</i>

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:36.240
<i>I don’t want Asu to have to go through that.</i>

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:41.950
<i>I’m here in Mom’s place, so I have to be there on parents’ day.</i>

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:47.030
<i>Even so, I don’t have anything appropriate to wear.</i>

00:05:58.450 --> 00:05:59.740
Onee-chan…

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:03.070
What are you doing?

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:05.300
Sorry, I didn’t mean to wake you.

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:09.650
What are you doing with all these clothes, Onee-chan?

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:12.810
For your parents’ day.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:19.610
You haven’t mentioned them in the past, so I’ve never gone to one.

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:21.430
I want to be there this year.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:26.190
Um, Onee-chan,

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:28.130
it’s fine if you don’t come.

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:28.740
Hmm?

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:30.950
It’s fine if you don’t come.

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:34.450
What?! You don’t want your big sister to go?!

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:36.590
Ah, no, that’s not it.

00:06:36.590 --> 00:06:39.270
It’s just that you have school too, right?

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:40.960
Ah, that’s right.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:45.690
Thank you, Onee-chan. It’s all right if you don’t come.

00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:47.720
Please don’t worry about it.

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:51.720
Anyway, if you don’t get some sleep, you’ll be too tired to deliver newspapers tomorrow morning.

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:53.140
Right?

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.690
Y-Yeah.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:02.260
<i>Even though she says it’s because I have school too,</i>

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:06.560
<i>all her classmates’ parents will be there, right?</i>

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:12.530
<i>Maybe she’s embarrassed that I’m just a middle-schooler.</i>

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:18.950
<i>If I had some clothes that would make me look more grown-up, I’d be fine.</i>

