00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:38.540
Th-This is…!

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:42.100
Asu!

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:46.230
Onee-chan, welcome home.

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:49.310
I found a w-wallet in front of our a-apartment!{stutter necessary?}

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:50.290
A wallet?

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:51.450
What should we do?

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:52.950
Wh-Wh-What should we do?

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:54.720
Calm down, Onee-chan.

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:58.440
Does it have anything with a name or an address in it?

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:10.420
There’s a ton of money in here!

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:11.290
Yeah.

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:15.120
With this much money,

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:20.630
we could pay the month’s rent, buy groceries, and get any cake that we want!

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:24.150
We could buy you some new clothes!

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:27.330
<i>That’s right! With this much money,</i>

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:31.520
<i>I’d be able to buy something grown-up to wear to parents’ day.</i>

00:08:36.350 --> 00:08:37.900
<i>No, no!</i>

00:08:38.260 --> 00:08:40.310
The person who lost this wallet is probably in trouble.

00:08:40.310 --> 00:08:42.060
Let’s take it to the police.

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:44.690
You need to go deliver the newspaper, right?

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:46.010
I can take it.

00:08:46.010 --> 00:08:47.120
Are you sure?

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:47.670
Yeah.

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:03.480
Are you really going to be okay?

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:04.770
I’ll be fine.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:07.240
You worry too much, Onee-chan.

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:11.970
You’re carrying around a fortune, so make sure you don’t go off with anyone suspicious.

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:12.990
Okay!

00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:28.820
Hey, you!

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:31.050
You’re the little sister from next door, right?

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:36.880
Ah, the lady from next door!

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:37.490
Hel—

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:41.100
I was the one who dropped that wallet. Give it back to me, will you?

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:46.010
<i>Suspicious…</i>

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:50.330
<i>Even though it’s someone we know, she still seems suspicious, Onee-san.</i>

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:55.860
Inside the wallet there’s an ID Card, right? The name is Saegusa Ranko.

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:00.710
You’re right!

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:05.530
I’m glad I was able to return it to you!

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:10.090
Little miss, from up close you’re awfully cute.

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:12.800
Let me thank you for this. Come on.

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:25.060
Mental math practice with
gram-to-price ratios improves grades.

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:25.060
Which is the

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:25.060
better bargain?

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:33.570
Gather together a lot of little
soap shavings to wash a big back.

00:10:43.470 --> 00:10:47.710
<i>A chocolate parfait, along with strawberry shortcake, and pudding à la mode!</i>

00:10:48.150 --> 00:10:50.860
Now, don’t be shy; eat up.

00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:52.420
O-Okay!

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:57.380
<i>Make sure you don’t go off with anyone suspicious.</i>

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:04.260
What’s wrong? You don’t like sweets?

00:11:05.270 --> 00:11:11.250
Onee-chan told me not to accept things from suspic—f-from people who I don’t know very well.

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:17.540
I guess these sunglasses make me look pretty shady, huh?

00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:18.570
Well then…

00:11:22.020 --> 00:11:23.790
<i>She looks like a nice person.</i>

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:29.580
Thanks for the food!

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:40.620
<i>Onee-chan would probably like to eat some of this cake, too.</i>

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:41.630
Hey,

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:43.930
you still won’t eat it?

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:49.500
Um, would it be okay to take this home instead?

00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:52.340
I’d like to split it with my big sister.

00:11:52.340 --> 00:11:53.740
The cake?

00:11:53.740 --> 00:11:54.360
Yes.

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:58.650
You can eat all that by yourself.

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:01.820
We can keep this as our little secret from your big sister.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:05.780
<i>All this, by myself?</i>

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:13.430
<i>We’d be able to buy Asu’s favorite cake, too!</i>

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:22.370
I think my big sister would do the same thing if she were in my shoes.

00:12:29.490 --> 00:12:33.000
Excuse me! Hey! Excuse me!

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:39.080
Thank you so much!

00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:40.580
You’re welcome.

00:12:46.050 --> 00:12:48.210
There’s something I’ve wanted to ask you since we last met.

00:12:48.210 --> 00:12:49.080
Yes?

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:53.990
You two… it’s just you and your sister living alone next door?

00:12:53.990 --> 00:12:54.730
Yes.

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:56.800
What about your mother and father?

00:12:57.780 --> 00:13:01.430
Dad is… living somewhere else.

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:06.230
Mom is… gone.

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:12.360
Sorry for asking such a strange question.

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:14.350
I was simply curious.{I was just concerned}

00:13:14.900 --> 00:13:15.900
It’s okay.

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:18.870
As long as Onee-chan is here with me, I’m fine.

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:20.630
I see.

00:13:20.630 --> 00:13:21.650
Yes.

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:27.610
But I do sometimes wonder why mom’s not here any more.

00:13:28.590 --> 00:13:30.580
Every once in a while.{Even though it’s just a thought…}

00:13:44.450 --> 00:13:46.480
Let’s dig in!

00:13:48.310 --> 00:13:49.660
Delicious!

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:50.680
So delicious!

00:13:51.050 --> 00:13:53.950
The lady next door is really a good person.

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:56.230
I’ll have to go thank her after we finish this!

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:57.980
Yes! I’ll come too!

00:13:58.460 --> 00:14:01.590
You already thanked her, so it’s okay.

00:14:01.590 --> 00:14:04.010
There’s still some tidying up to do after dinner, anyway.

00:14:04.010 --> 00:14:05.940
Well, okay.

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:07.820
Leave it to me!

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:12.500
Thank you for the cake.

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:16.580
Asu also thought it was delicious.

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:19.880
Oh my, you’re awfully cute too, now that I get a good look.

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:23.760
From now on, let’s be friends, okay?

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:24.910
Ah, sure.

00:14:24.910 --> 00:14:25.920
Well, see you later.

00:14:30.290 --> 00:14:33.470
<i>Compared to the person who yelled at us for being too loud,</i>

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:35.690
<i>she seems like a completely different person.</i>

00:14:36.310 --> 00:14:39.100
<i>It would be great if I could become a grown-up like her.</i>

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:44.150
<i>I’d be able to attend parents’ day without embarrassing Asu.</i>

00:14:45.330 --> 00:14:45.980
Um…

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:46.800
Yes?

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:50.170
This might be a rude thing to ask, but…

00:14:50.170 --> 00:14:50.950
What is it?

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:54.500
If you have any suits, could you please lend me one?

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:55.540
A suit?

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:57.630
I do have a few, but what do you need one for?

00:14:57.630 --> 00:15:00.540
I want to go to parents’ day for my sister!

00:15:01.010 --> 00:15:02.690
I want to fill in for mom,

00:15:03.230 --> 00:15:05.320
but I need something more formal to wear!

00:15:06.020 --> 00:15:07.010
Please!

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:12.800
But I do sometimes wonder why mom’s not here any more.

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:19.040
If that’s how it is, I’ll lend you as many suits as you want!

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:21.020
Th-Thank you so much!

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:22.020
Here, come on in.

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:24.470
Y-Yes! With pleasure!

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:33.280
For parents’ day at a primary school, you shouldn’t wear anything too revealing.

00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:35.540
<i>Mountains of garbage?</i>

00:15:36.990 --> 00:15:39.490
It’s a little messy, but don’t mind it.

00:15:40.070 --> 00:15:43.000
Maybe a light pink, or perhaps blue?

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:49.070
<i>I wonder what Saegusa-san does…</i>

00:15:49.070 --> 00:15:50.300
Alright!

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:52.100
This one should do it.

00:15:53.520 --> 00:15:55.570
What do you think?

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:04.350
It’s amazing!

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:08.210
It looks great on you! You look very mature.

00:16:08.210 --> 00:16:09.400
Really?

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:11.860
Yes, really. Have some confidence!

00:16:18.100 --> 00:16:21.140
Finally, put on a little bit of perfume, and…

00:16:21.140 --> 00:16:22.430
Perfect.

00:16:22.430 --> 00:16:23.970
Thank you very much.

00:16:23.970 --> 00:16:26.530
I’ll make sure to get them cleaned.

00:16:26.530 --> 00:16:28.250
Don’t you worry about that.

00:16:28.490 --> 00:16:30.390
I’ll let you hold on to them until tomorrow.{Tomorrow I’ll help put some makeup on you.}

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:34.880
How about it?

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:37.090
Wh-What happened, Onee-chan?

00:16:37.090 --> 00:16:38.890
I borrowed this from the lady next door!

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:42.480
Y-You put on perfume, too?

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:43.670
Yup.

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:46.290
This way I can take over for Mom, right?

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:49.290
Onee-chan.

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:49.940
Yes?

00:16:50.540 --> 00:16:53.100
Don’t force yourself to come to parents’ day.

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:54.620
What?

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:56.130
Asu…

00:16:57.410 --> 00:16:59.030
I’m not forcing myself…

00:16:59.730 --> 00:17:02.580
Ah! Oh no, the bath will close soon.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:04.410
Onee-chan, let’s go.

00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:05.660
Ah, okay.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:11.260
Bath House Hawaii{銭湯ハワイ}

00:17:16.570 --> 00:17:19.560
Don’t force yourself to come to parents’ day.

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:23.050
<i>I guess I’m no good after all.</i>

00:17:32.590 --> 00:17:35.920
<i>Too bad… back to same old me.</i>

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:45.030
Thank goodness.

00:17:47.780 --> 00:17:49.960
It’s Onee-chan’s usual smell.

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:54.240
Onee-chan, stop trying to
take someone else’s place.

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:57.870
You’re my older sister.

00:17:58.340 --> 00:17:59.810
Stay that way.

00:18:00.980 --> 00:18:02.780
Just keep being your normal self.

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:08.690
Ok. I will.

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:24.520
<i>In order to protect Asu from that same lonely and painful memory,</i>

00:18:24.520 --> 00:18:30.580
<i>I wanted to dress up and take Mother’s place on parents’ day.</i>

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:36.550
<i>But now I realize that the reason I wanted to act and dress like an adult</i>

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:42.510
<i>was mostly because I was afraid of being embarrassed myself.</i>

00:18:43.860 --> 00:18:45.450
<i>Looking at Asu’s face,</i>

00:18:45.450 --> 00:18:49.970
<i>it seems like she’s really trying hard to fight back her loneliness.</i>

00:18:58.330 --> 00:19:00.630
Asu-chan, who are you looking for?

00:19:00.630 --> 00:19:02.520
Oh, nobody in particular.

00:19:04.250 --> 00:19:06.120
There’s no way she’ll come.

00:19:08.650 --> 00:19:10.580
Class is starting!

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:17.800
Today is parents’ day, and all your parents are here. Everyone, just try to act the same as usual.

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:17.800
The writing here is the kanji for autumn (秋) with “Grade 3, class 1” (三年一組) written on the side, above the name of the student.

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:30.270
Oh my, who’s that? A middle school student?

00:19:33.590 --> 00:19:36.690
<i>If Asu wants me to stay just the way I am,</i>

00:19:37.160 --> 00:19:39.410
<i>then there’s no reason for me to be embarrassed.</i>

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:54.960
Well then, Yamada-san, can you read for us from page 94?

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:56.960
Y-Yes!

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:05.240
In the end, Taro said,

00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:12.710
“We can all definitely look forward to both the happy times and the sad times,

00:20:11.780 --> 00:20:13.520
<i>I’m here to observe you.</i>

00:20:12.970 --> 00:20:17.590
as these are feelings that come from the very bottom of your heart…”

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:21.700
<i>I always regret it when I don’t recognize Asu’s true feelings.</i>

00:20:22.730 --> 00:20:27.210
<i>But I’m watching her with my own eyes,</i>

00:20:27.880 --> 00:20:29.240
<i>and striving to protect her.</i>

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:33.850
<i>If that makes Asu feel safe and happy,</i>

00:20:33.850 --> 00:20:37.620
<i>I’m definitely keeping my promise to you,</i>

00:20:37.620 --> 00:20:39.580
<i>right, Mom?</i>

00:20:42.790 --> 00:20:45.520
Hey, Onee-chan, what did you do about school?

00:20:46.230 --> 00:20:47.610
I just left early.

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:53.270
{小学校}

00:20:49.690 --> 00:20:50.860
Onee-chan.

00:20:51.420 --> 00:20:52.260
Yeah?

00:20:54.090 --> 00:20:55.020
Thank you.

00:20:58.070 --> 00:20:59.260
The truth is…

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:05.760
The truth is, I really did want you to come!

00:21:08.750 --> 00:21:11.120
I knew that all along!

00:21:13.190 --> 00:21:14.120
Geez.{are this and its predecessor really necessary}

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:20.460
All right! Next time you have a class visit, I’m going to be there.

00:21:20.460 --> 00:21:23.030
Hey now, I’m not so sure about that.

00:21:23.030 --> 00:21:24.400
Huh? Why not?

